<main class="bio-page">
  <section class="bio-hero">
    <div class="bio-hero-grid">
      <div class="bio-hero-copy">
        <p class="bio-location">Berlin · digital and media artist</p>
        <h1>Gleb<br>Kalinin</h1>
        <p class="bio-deck">Images, systems, situations.</p>
        <p class="bio-intro">I work with digital media, interactive installations, artistic research and experiments that do not fit neatly inside conventional software development. The same practice moves into clubs, classrooms, workshops and conversations with people and teams.</p>
        <a class="bio-down" href="#practice">Enter the story <span>↓</span></a>
      </div>
      <figure class="bio-portrait bio-portrait--hero">
        <img src="/images/202301-glebkalinin.jpg" alt="Black-and-white portrait of Gleb Kalinin" width="800" height="814">
        <figcaption>Gleb Kalinin · Berlin</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bio-manifesto" id="practice">
    <h2 class="bio-statement">Not one discipline, but a way of moving between <em>image, code, sound, bodies and attention.</em></h2>
    <div class="bio-practice-grid">
      <article><h3>Art &amp; performance</h3><p>Digital media, interactive installations, photography, music and performance in clubs.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Research &amp; experiments</h3><p>Artistic research and working prototypes that test how emerging technologies change everyday life.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Teaching &amp; workshops</h3><p>Learning spaces where people build with new tools, compare methods and develop their own practice.</p></article>
      <article><h3>People &amp; teams</h3><p>Consulting, coaching, one-to-one work and collaboration with teams around products, attention and change.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bio-story">
    <header class="bio-story-head">
      <h2>From the early web<br>to thinking machines</h2>
      <p>These chapters overlap. Together they form a long-running inquiry into media, tools, people and the forms that connect them.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="bio-eras">
      <article class="bio-era"><p class="bio-era-date">2001—2010</p><div><h3>Learning the internet by making it</h3><p>Gleb launched his first internet project, Experiment.ru, in 2001. He later became the initiator and first editor-in-chief of Theory and Practice in Saint Petersburg, building the editorial team and organising around twenty events.</p></div></article>
      <article class="bio-era"><p class="bio-era-date">2010—2018</p><div><h3>Studios, products and communities</h3><p>He ran Raum7, a consultancy working across UX and design; co-founded the neighbourhood network Lokolo; worked on services for Russian Post at Tsentsiper; and later led content at Ostrovok.ru.</p></div></article>
      <article class="bio-era"><p class="bio-era-date">2016—2020</p><div><h3>Leadership with the human in focus</h3><p>Gleb served as curator of the Moscow Global Shapers hub and as product director at OZON.travel. Alongside product work, his interest in attention, behaviour and group learning became an increasingly public part of his practice.</p></div></article>
      <article class="bio-era bio-era--now"><p class="bio-era-date">2020—now</p><div><h3>An independent, expanded practice</h3><p>Based in Berlin, he works independently across AI, mental-health technology, artistic experimentation, consulting and education. His current laboratories bring people together to build personal systems and new ways of working with AI.</p></div></article>
    </div>
  </section>

